    <tok fileIndex="0" linenr="361" column="3" str="/*x   * Sending the encryption type in clear seems wrong. It should bex   * protected with gss_seal()/gss_wrap(). See RFC1961 extract belowx   * The NEC reference implementations on which this is based isx   * therefore at faultx   *x   *  +------+------+------+.......................+x   *  + ver  | mtyp | len  |   token               |x   *  +------+------+------+.......................+x   *  + 0x01 | 0x02 | 0x02 | up to 2^16 - 1 octets |x   *  +------+------+------+.......................+x   *x   *   Where:x   *x   *  - &quot;ver&quot; is the protocol version number, here 1 to represent thex   *    first version of the SOCKS/GSS-API protocolx   *x   *  - &quot;mtyp&quot; is the message type, here 2 to represent a protectionx   *    -level negotiation messagex   *x   *  - &quot;len&quot; is the length of the &quot;token&quot; field in octetsx   *x   *  - &quot;token&quot; is the GSS-API encapsulated protection levelx   *x   * The token is produced by encapsulating an octet containing thex   * required protection level using gss_seal()/gss_wrap() with conf_reqx   * set to FALSE. The token is verified using gss_unseal()/x   * gss_unwrap().x   *x   */"/>
